 /*
- * Automatic frame extension. The exposure control advertises up to a 24 fps
- * frame, and the driver lengthens VTS whenever a request no longer fits, so
- * AE can trade frame rate for light without driving VBLANK itself. With AE
- * raising exposure before gain, dim scenes drop towards 24 fps with 25% more
- * light per frame, and bright scenes stay at 30 fps.
+ * Frame timing. Measured on this sensor unless noted:
+ *   - V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE counts rows, registers 0x3e00-0x3e02 count half rows.
+ *   - The init table runs a two-exposure readout whose short exposure owns
+ *     SC200PC_SHORT_WINDOW rows of every frame (0x3e23/0x3e24), so the
+ *     exposure register must not exceed SC200PC_EXPOSURE_REG_MAX(VTS). Past
+ *     that the sensor lengthens the frame on its own, whatever VTS says.
+ *   - VTS is even and never below the init table's, as in the OEM Windows
+ *     driver.
+ *   - Exposure, gain and VTS writes take effect on the next frame. Inside a
+ *     register group (0x3812) they take a frame longer and are dropped when
+ *     another group opens before then, so of two control writes in one frame
+ *     the first is lost. Hence plain writes, one transfer per register so the
+ *     sensor never latches one half written.
+ * VBLANK asks for a frame length and the driver lengthens it, down to 15 fps,
+ * as far as the exposure needs.
  */
